# Day 18 — Phase E: previews, Skim mode, faster quick views

Goal (spec §17): holding the wheel never builds up lag.

## What was found first

The 108 MP photos (IMG_20241126_2004xx–2019xx, 12000 x 9000) and the 12 MP ones of the same day have **no EXIF thumbnail**. The older phone photos have one (P_2023…: 190 x 107, IMG_2023…: 256 x 144). Previews therefore help many files, but not the biggest ones; for those the quick view itself had to get faster (WIC, below).

## Changes

**Preview quality (spec §7.1).** New unit `source\imaging\uJpegHeader.pas`: reads only the start of a JPEG (marker segments up to the frame header) with a file stream: size, EXIF orientation and the EXIF thumbnail. `uExifOrientation` finds the thumbnail (IFD1, tags 0x0201 / 0x0202). The loader decodes it (qlPreview), turns it upright and cuts off black bars when its shape differs from the photo (many cameras store 160 x 120 for 16:9). Files without a thumbnail answer "No preview in this file"; MView remembers them and doesn't ask again.

**Wanted set.**
- Current image, nothing cached: Preview and Screen, both P0. The thumbnail shows within a few ms and is replaced by the quick view without changing the view (Preview -> Screen -> Full).
- Previews of the next `PreviewAhead` images (default 10), first among the preloads: they cost a header read each.
- Screen preloads as before (a cached thumbnail doesn't count as preloaded).

**Skim mode (spec §6).** Steps less than 1/`SkimRate` s apart (default 4 per second) for `SkimEnterMs` (1500 ms) switch to Skim:
- only previews are wanted (current and ahead); no Screen or Full decodes, no Screen preloads;
- files without a thumbnail still get a Screen decode, which the next step cancels;
- the info line says "skimming", the D line "SKIM" (otherwise "browse").
`SkimExitMs` (250 ms) without a step, or a slow step, switches back: the image you stopped at gets its quick view at once, full size after RefineDelayMs.
The directory scan is not paused in Skim (spec §5.2 S2); not needed so far.

**Quick views with WIC (`UseWICQuickView=1`).** WIC decodes JPEGs scaled to 1/2 … 1/8 inside the codec (IWICBitmapSourceTransform), like pasjpeg's DCT scaling but expected several times faster (full size: WIC 1 s vs pasjpeg 6.1 s for 108 MP). One call, so it can't be cancelled midway (expected 0.1–0.3 s). CMYK and other formats WIC can't scale fall back to the own decoder.

**Review fixes (independent review):** Skim now always ends properly after a slow step, also when the step doesn't move; a broken file whose thumbnail was readable shows its error (and is skipped with PlaceholderForBadImages=0), not the thumbnail; room is kept for the quick view still to come; overflow guard for huge scaled WIC images.

## Settings ([Performance], with balloon help in the editor)

`PreviewAhead=10`, `SkimEnterMs=1500` (0 = never skim), `SkimRate=4`, `SkimExitMs=250`, `UseWICQuickView=1`. The editor adds them to MView.ini when it opens.

## Tests

TestExif: 40 checks expected (20 new): header, size, orientation and thumbnail of the four new pictures in `test\images\thumb` (made with Python, checked with Pillow; thumb_orient6 uses big-endian EXIF), no thumbnail in orient_1, missing file; AspectCrop (same shape, 16:9 and 9:16 in 160 x 120, under 2 % off, empty).

`test\images\thumb`: open `thumb_plain.jpg` in MView: for a moment you may see the red "THUMB" picture before the blue "MAIN IMAGE" (small files decode fast, so it can be too quick to see). `thumb_letterbox.jpg`: the red preview must fill the frame without black bars.

